              "content": "Saved dashboard views now persist and restore the way you specified. `npm run gate` (lint, typecheck, all tests) passes with 33/33 tests, and `npm run build` succeeds.\n\n**What changed:** the only production file edited is `src/domain/Saved_View.ts`. `App.tsx` already loaded the view on startup and saved it on every click, so it needed no changes.\n- **Saving:** each selection, including `all`, is written straight away as its exact string under `dashboard.saved-view`.\n- **Restoring:** only the exact strings `all`, `active` and `archived` are accepted. No trimming, case changes or JSON.\n- **Absent, empty or invalid values:** the dashboard shows `all` and leaves storage untouched. A bad value is only overwritten when the user next picks a view.\n- **Storage errors:** if `getItem` throws, the dashboard silently shows `all`. If `setItem` throws, the selected view still applies on screen and nothing is thrown or shown. No new storage API or error UI.\n\n**Tests:** I added two new test files and left the existing ones byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- `src/domain/Saved_View_Persistence.test.ts` checks the rules directly: valid and invalid values, not writing on load, the stored format, save then load, and both storage errors.\n- `src/App_Persistence.test.tsx` renders the real app to check restore on reload, the default on first visit, that an invalid value is left alone, that each click is saved, and both storage errors.\n\nI ran the new tests before implementing and they failed against the stubs, as expected. Package metadata, build config, check scripts and the other test files are unchanged.\n\nThe work is on a new branch, `feat/saved-view-persistence`, and is **not committed yet**. Tell me if you'd like me to commit it and open a PR.",
